hadiths[5]{hadithnumber,text}:
"22286","Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Zayd, Umayr, the freedman of Abi al-Lahm, narrated to me, he said: I witnessed Khaybar with my masters, and they spoke about me to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he ordered me and I was girded with a sword, and I dragged it. He was informed that I am a slave, so he ordered for me something from the inferior baggage."
"22287","Ribi ibn Ibrahim, the brother of Ismail Ibn Ulayya, and he praised him well, and he used to excel over Ismail, narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Zayd ibn al-Muhajir, from Umayr, the freedman of Abi al-Lahm, he said: I witnessed Khaybar with my masters, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered me and I was girded with a sword, and I dragged it. He said: So it was said to him: He is an owned slave. He said: So he ordered for me something from the inferior baggage. He said: And I showed him a ruqya with which I used to treat the mad in the Jahiliyya. He said: Cast such and such from it, and treat with what remains. Muhammad ibn Zayd said: And I met him while he was treating the mad with it."
"22288","Ribi ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman, meaning Ibn Ishaq, narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from his uncle, and from Muhammad ibn Zayd ibn al-Muhajir, that they heard Umayr, the freedman of Abi al-Lahm, he said: I came with my masters wanting the Hijra until when we neared Madina, he said: They entered Madina and left me behind them. He said: Severe hunger afflicted me. He said: Some of those who go out from Madina passed by me and said to me: Had you entered Madina, you would have gotten from the fruits of its gardens. I entered a garden and cut two clusters, and the owner of the garden came and brought me to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and informed him of my story, and upon me were two garments. He said to me: Which of them is better? I pointed to one of them for him. He said: Take it and give the owner of the garden the other, and he released me."
"22290","Harun ibn Maruf narrated to us, he said: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Haywa said, from Ibn al-Had, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Taymi, from Umayr, the freedman of Abi al-Lahm, that he saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, praying for rain at the stones of oil, near al-Zawra, standing supplicating, seeking rain, raising his hands, not exceeding his head with them, turning the insides of his hands toward his face."
"22291","Harun narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: And Haywa informed me, from Umar ibn Malik, from Ibn al-Had, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Umayr, the freedman of Abi al-Lahm, that he saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he mentioned the like of it."
